  "name": "Bhuta kola paddana (Tulu spirit-worship epic song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bhuta kola (daiva kola) is the night-long spirit-worship ritual of the Tulu-speaking coast of Karnataka, in which a performer from the Pambada, Nalike or Parava communities embodies the daiva. Paddanas, the Tulu oral epics of the spirits and culture heroes, are sung at the rituals and in the paddy fields; Lauri Honko's Folklore Fellows team recorded singer Gopala Naika's Siri epic. The drum card stands in for the tembare, the drum that accompanies paddana singing.",
  "recipe": "classic modern bhuta kola paddana, ritual Devotional, hindu branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
